# Identity Center group membership for platform permission sets.
#
# Copy to config/identity.env and fill in. That file is gitignored: it holds
# personal data (names and direct email addresses) and must not enter version
# control. The pre-commit hook blocks it.
#
# Group DISPLAY NAMES are not personal data and live in the repository — the
# defaults below are correct and should not normally be changed. Only the
# member lists belong here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Member list format
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   GivenName|FamilyName|email[|userName][,GivenName|FamilyName|email...]
#
# Pipes within a record, commas between records. Neither character is legal in
# an email address, so the format cannot be ambiguous. Whitespace around any
# field is stripped.
#
#   COMMERCIAL_READONLY_MEMBERS="Ada|Lovelace|ada@example.com,Alan|Turing|alan@example.com"
#
# The email doubles as the Identity Center user name — the thing the person
# signs in with at the access portal — which is also what SCIM will key on
# after the Entra cutover.
#
# The optional FOURTH field overrides that user name. It exists for people
# whose directory entry predates this script and does not use their email:
#
#   COMMERCIAL_READONLY_MEMBERS="Ada|Lovelace|ada@example.com|ada"
#
# Use it only to point at an EXISTING user. Without it, a lookup by email
# returns nothing for such a person and the script creates a second identity
# for them alongside the first — two users, one human, and only one of them
# in the group. Prefer fixing the directory to fixing the config; the override
# is a bridge, not a convention.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file has a shelf life
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# It exists because the Identity Center identity source is still the built-in
# directory, so users and groups have to be created somewhere. Once the source
# is switched to Entra, SCIM provisions both from Entra group membership and
# this file becomes the wrong place to change access. Delete it then; do not
# keep two sources of truth for who has access to what.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CommercialReadOnly — billing and cost data only (design doc 12)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AltDigital commercial function. Full portfolio, all partners, all clients.
# A partner-scoped variant for partner business users is prompt 14.5 and does
# not exist yet — do not put partner staff in this group.
COMMERCIAL_READONLY_GROUP="CommercialReadOnly"
COMMERCIAL_READONLY_MEMBERS=""

# Security function. Estate-wide READ access to security controls, findings and
# evidence -- no write anywhere, no secret values, no decryption, no role
# assumption. identity/30-security-readonly.yaml is the permission set;
# scripts/deploy-security-access.sh creates the group, the people and the
# per-account assignments.
#
# Same record format as above: GivenName|FamilyName|email[|userName],
# comma-separated between records. The optional fourth field references a user
# created before these scripts existed, so an existing identity is reused
# rather than a duplicate created alongside it.
#
# Empty is a valid state and is the first-run case: the group, the permission
# set and every assignment can exist before anybody is in it, so adding a
# person later is one line here and a re-run rather than a deployment.
SECURITY_READONLY_GROUP="SecurityReadOnly"
SECURITY_READONLY_MEMBERS=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auditors — AuditEvidenceReader, for the length of an audit engagement
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything SecurityReadOnly sees, plus the evidence itself: archived
# CloudTrail (and the Athena workgroup over it), platform log contents, the
# evidence tables and execution history. identity/40-audit-evidence-reader.yaml
# is the permission set; scripts/deploy-audit-access.sh creates the group, the
# people, the trail query stack and the per-account assignments.
#
# A SEPARATE group from SecurityReadOnly on purpose. That group holds every
# quorum approver; this one holds whoever is examining the platform, including
# an external assessor, and only while they are.
#
# AUDIT_ENGAGEMENT_ENDS is REQUIRED to grant, as YYYY-MM-DD. The script refuses
# to grant without it or past it. It does NOT revoke on that date -- run
#   scripts/deploy-audit-access.sh --end-engagement
# when the engagement closes. Extending is changing the date and re-running;
# the config change is the record that someone decided to extend.
AUDITORS_GROUP="Auditors"
AUDITORS_MEMBERS=""
AUDIT_ENGAGEMENT_ENDS=""
